# ❤️ Heart Disease Prediction App (KNN Model)

This project is a **Machine Learning-based web application** that predicts the risk of heart disease based on patient health parameters.  
The app is built with **Streamlit** and uses a pre-trained **K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)** model for predictions.

---

## 📊 Model Performance

| Metric                | Value   |
|-----------------------|---------|
| **Algorithm**         | K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN) |
| **Best K**            | 9 (determined via 10-fold CV over K=1 to 20) |
| **Training Accuracy** | **74.4%** |
| **Test Accuracy**     | **80.2%** |

---

## 📌 Features
- Predicts **High Risk** or **Low Risk** of heart disease.
- Shows **probability score** for better interpretability.
- User-friendly interface with input validation.
- Works instantly — no retraining required.
- Supports scaling of features to ensure accurate predictions.

---

---

## 🧠 Model Information
- **Dataset:** [UCI Heart Disease Dataset](https://archive.ics.uci.edu/ml/datasets/heart+Disease)  
- **Algorithm:** **K-Nearest Neighbors (KNN)**
- **Hyperparameter tuning:** 10-fold Cross-Validation, K values from 1 to 20.
- **Best K:** 9
- **Features Used:**
  - `age` – Age of the patient
  - `sex` – Gender (1 = Male, 0 = Female)
  - `cp` – Chest pain type (0–3)
  - `trestbps` – Resting blood pressure (mm Hg)
  - `chol` – Serum cholesterol (mg/dl)
  - `thalach` – Maximum heart rate achieved
  - `oldpeak` – ST depression induced by exercise
  - `slope` – Slope of the peak exercise ST segment
  - `ca` – Number of major vessels (0–3)
  - `thal` – Thalassemia (0–2)
- **Target Variable:** `target` (1 = Heart disease present, 0 = Not present)
- **Preprocessing:** StandardScaler applied to numeric features.

